        "text": "Lilou Chloé Perrine Wadoux-Ducellier (born 10 April 2001) is a French professional racing driver. She is a Ferrari factory driver, and the first woman to win an FIA World Endurance Championship race. Wadoux is also an IMSA GTD champion, LMP2 race winner and Hypercar test driver. Wadoux made her WEC debut for Richard Mille's team in 2022, before joining AF Corse and Ferrari in 2023.",
